DESCRIPTION:Learn where and how to search for books\, articles\, and more.
   We’ll break down the differences between primary and secondary sources.
   We'll discuss "credible sources\," both those from scholarly (peer-revi
 ewed) journals and those from other sources.  We'll also discuss\, among 
 other things\, the differences between our two largest family of database
 s -- ProQuest and EBSCO. We want you to advance your searching skills so 
 that you learn to have fun searching (a.k.a. researching). A perfect work
 shop if you’re new to college-level research or you just want to sharpen 
 your skills before your next assignment.\nRegister Here: https://montclai
 r.libcal.com/event/17454788\n\nHosted by: Sprague Library\n\nOnline Locat
 ion: https://montclair.libcal.com/event/17454788\n\nAdditional Informatio
 n can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12600612
