DESCRIPTION:Join us for a hands-on workshop where educators explore how me
 dia shapes storytelling\, identity\, and representation. Through the New 
 Jersey Hall of Fame\, educators will explore exhibits spanning different 
 historical media breakthroughs. From news anchor Connie Chung\, to Thomas
  Edison’s invention of the first camera\, to the iconic music of Whitney 
 Houston— educators will become experts in multiple avenues of media produ
 ction\, bringing media literacy directly into their classroom. They will 
 choose a project to develop\, apply learned skills through Canva\, and le
 ave ready to support students through podcasts\, reels\, or digital short
 s tied to New Jersey.\n\nHosted by: The ADP Center\n\nOnline Location: ht
 tps://www.google.com/url?q=https://montclair.zoom.us/j/93884432229?pwd%3D
 VDwPg3hF2CT6G3Nkp1c37y9pwk0DDq.1&sa=D&source=calendar&ust=177774913537436
 1&usg=AOvVaw1GyIj76zsn01Byq4Xan-5z\n\nAdditional Information can be found
  at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12714205
