 ed for a good time! Event: Mini-Japanese Autumn Festival \nTime: 1:45 - 3
 :15 pm \nDate: Wed. November 18 \nLocation: Schmitt Hall\, Room125 \nProg
 ram: Only at the Mini-Japanese Autumn Festival! \n\nMake your own onigiri
  with spicy tuna or pickled vegetables Or\, Ramen with sautéed chicken an
 d vegetables Takoyaki with octopus\, salmon\, cheese pearls and broccoli 
 \nNot in the mood for making any? No problem! There will be yakisoba and 
 okonomiyaki waiting for you. \nWhat else? Kendama and chopstick games to 
 play for a good time and prizes! \nDraw with a brush dipped in ink… Make 
 an origami crane for Happy Holidays! \n\nAll for free! \nThe Festival is 
 brought to you by the Japanese Language Circle and the Japan Club Sponsor
 ed by the Department of Global Cultural Studies\, CHSS\n\nHosted by: Coll
 ege of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS)\n\nAdditional Information ca
 n be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12980251
