DESCRIPTION:Join us for a screening of Sweet Country (2017)\, directed by 
 Aboriginal Australian filmmaker Warwick Thornton. Set in Australia's Nort
 hern Territory in 1929\, the film explores the experiences of Aboriginal 
 Australians under colonial rule and raises important questions about just
 ice\, racism\, cultural identity\, and belonging.\nThis screening invites
  students to broaden their global perspectives\, reflect on international
  Indigenous histories and engage in meaningful cross-cultural dialogue.\n
 Refreshments will be provided.\nCo-sponsored by University Libraries\, th
 e Office of Global Engagement\, and International Academic Initiatives\nR
 egister Here: https://montclair.libcal.com/event/17876749\n\nHosted by: S
 prague Library\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montcla
 ir.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12918411
