DESCRIPTION:LAIC (LATIN AMERICAN INDIGENOUS COLLABORATIVE) at CLaSE invite
 s the Montclair State University community and the broader public to part
 icipate in our Kichwa Language & Culture Workshop Series\, beginning Mond
 ay\, September 14.\nThis 10-week workshop series offers participants the 
 opportunity to learn Kichwa while exploring the language\, culture\, and 
 traditions of Kichwa-speaking communities. Workshops are conducted in Spa
 nish and Kichwa by our amazing and well known Kichwa community leaders - 
 Atik Paguay and Fabian Muenala and are open to students\, faculty\, staff
 \, families\, and community members from outside the University. No previ
 ous knowledge of Kichwa is required.\nMondays\, beginning September 145:3
 0–7:30 p.m.Cole Hall\, Room 14110-week series\nWe invite everyone interes
 ted in Indigenous languages and cultures to join us. Registration is requ
 ired by contacting Dr. Calarota-Ninman at  calarotaa@montclair.edu\n\nHos
 ted by: Center for Latino Heritage & Spanish Language Excellence\n\nAddit
 ional Information can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engag
 e/event/12663590
DTEND:20261124T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20261114T061455Z
DTSTART:20261123T223000Z
