BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:Arts
DESCRIPTION:Maurice Ravel’s L’enfant et les sortilèges is a wildly imagina
 tive fantasy opera where a single child’s tantrum sets an entire enchante
 d world into motion. In a flash of frustration\, the ordinary becomes ext
 raordinary—walls start to whisper\, teacups burst into song\, animals arg
 ue back\, and the child’s room transforms into a living\, breathing world
  of magic and mischief.\nAs this fantastical realm awakens\, the child is
  swept into a dazzling swirl of musical surprises and unexpected voices\,
  where every object has something to say and nothing is quite as it seems
 . With Ravel’s shimmering\, kaleidoscopic score at its heart\, this encha
 nting opera is a playful journey through wonder\, chaos\, and the power o
 f imagination to transform everything it touches.\n(Sung in French with E
 nglish Surtitles~ runtime: approx 1 hour)\nMontclair State University Stu
 dents FREE with ID at Kasser Box Office\n\nHosted by: The College of the 
 Arts\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.campusl
 abs.com/engage/event/12657859
DTEND:20261206T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261114T061455Z
DTSTART:20261206T220000Z
LOCATION:Alexander Kasser Theater
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
